Scope note: this license covers the code and original documentation in this
repository. Captured documents under data/captures/ remain the property of
their respective publishers. The corpus comprises (i) public summaries and
related documents published under Article 53 of Regulation (EU) 2024/1689,
(ii) the European Commission's official template documents, (iii) pages
and files captured from the locations where providers publish such documents
(portals, catalogs, bundled document sets), and (iv) copies of pages and
archived documents from third-party public trackers and archives (notably the
AI Accountability Lab's tracker and write-once archives), captured with
attribution so the provenance chain includes its own upstream sources — all
archived for public-interest transparency and research, with attribution,
alongside verification metadata.
Documents served as files are archived unmodified; JavaScript-rendered pages
are archived as a rendered DOM and marked as derived in their manifests.
Capture manifests, hashes, and the events log are released under CC0.
